{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier model normalizes each retrieval summary to unit weight, while DIN’s primary paper explicitly preserves activation magnitude. That suggests a focused follow-up: test whether field summaries benefit from retaining target-dependent magnitude.\n\nI’ll implement four variants with identical parameters: an unchanged softmax reference, normalized sigmoid pooling, count-scaled sigmoid pooling, and unnormalized sigmoid pooling. Their contrasts will separate the scoring function, history-count scaling, and target-dependent magnitude. This is a testable adaptation of a known idea; novelty and effectiveness remain unverified."}}
