 causes, and the subgrouped branch remains a recorded negative trajectory.',\n 'Earlier knowledge usage declared EST-style field identity consideration but did not implement iterative event-state updates; those prior runs support at most a small field-retrieval effect and do not validate EST or knowledge usefulness. Previously rejected Zenith/UltraHSTU/SSR directions remain unevaluated, not scientifically refuted.',\n 'Official offline history visibility, whole-window vocabularies/static snapshots and category/brand-based auxiliary labels limit production and advertisement-conversion interpretations.'\n],\n'contrasts':[],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g0-r0000-field_global wall 325.231653s, training 293.755228s, inference 25.294572s; baseline-din wall 328.913273s; runtime protocol conservative estimated_unit_seconds 481.347588 and trial cap 1203.368969s. Remaining research wall at contract resolution 169076.881228s; all subsequent preparation and scoring costs count.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Four full-protocol runs, no subset screening: conservative 4*481.347588=1925.390352s, cap-based exposure 4*1203.368969=4813.475876s. Reserve at least 8000s for any failed attempts, host forward/backward/masking checks, attribution diagnostics and future paired repetitions of a consequential candidate and closest controls. Target three paired seeds if a later authorized host phase supports them; no seed/recipe override in these configs.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Keep at least 10000s for freezing and host-managed final suite assessment/repetition; withheld scoring remains closed in this phase. Freeze source/config/checkpoint hashes, chosen candidates, DIN/closest controls and assessment commands before any assessment request. No held-out request is made here.',\n 'stop_rule':'Do not train or install in the coding jail. Only prepare four standalone modules and proposal; host executes under the frozen interface. Each reference rerun, check, control, failure or retry consumes the same ledger. Do not exceed the host 1203.368969s per-trial cap, campaign deadline or remaining budget; unknown execution state does not authorize a duplicate. Stop on integrity failure or when no useful experiment fits while preserving reserves. A nonpositive contrast is a valid result and cannot justify changing the protocol.'\n}}\ncontrasts=[\n ('mass_sum versus count_scaled','mass_sum: unnormalized sigmoid weights, total mass M[b,f]','count_scaled: identical relative sigmoid weights with target-independent mass N/2','Target-dependent mass beyond count','Follow with paired host-managed repetitions of mass_sum/count_scaled and normalized reference if click gain >=0.001; report residual optimization confounds.','If count scaling explains the gain, report that evidence and do not attribute value to target-dependent intensity.'),\n ('mass_sum versus mass_normalized','mass_sum retains total sigmoid activation mass','mass_normalized divides identical gates by their total mass','Retaining magnitude','Use count_scaled contrast to discriminate count from target-specific effects before claiming mechanism support.','Retain negative result and consider the unchanged projection bottleneck only in a subsequent prospective study.'),\n ('count_scaled versus mass_normalized','count_scaled multiplies the normalized summary by N/2','mass_normalized has unit total weight for nonempty histories','History-count-linked scaling','Describe a count-linked or optimization effect; target intensity requires the separate primary contrast.','Do not assume every unnormalized-pooling benefit comes from count.'),\n ('mass_normalized versus softmax_reference','Normalized sigmoid kernel','Original masked softmax kernel','Kernel replacement','If only this comparison wins, attribute provisional support to the kernel family, not magnitude.','A null kernel effect makes the mass contrasts easier to interpret but does not prove an intensity mechanism.'),\n ('softmax_reference versus g0-r0000-field_global','Faithful from-scratch rerun of the same reference pathway','Committed parent trial and source/config identity','Execution consistency','Use both receipts as provenance; a same-seed rerun is not an independent repetition.','Investigate implementation/protocol identity; suspend causal interpretation of the whole suite if mismatch is material.')\n]\nfor name,intervention,control,purpose,yes,no in contrasts:\n study['contrasts'].append({'parent_ref':'g0-r0000-field_global','intervention':name+': '+intervention,'control':control,'held_fixed':['Inputs, official_offline visibility, all labels, history limit 100, full split/scorers', 'Same field retrieval, no feedback grouping, log counts and absence flags', 'All trainable tensors, initialization order, parameter counts, token/readout structure', 'One pass, seed 20262027, batch 8192, split optimizers/rates, BCE sum, precision and host limits'], 'remaining_confounds':[purpose+' is tested under finite single-pass optimization; normalization also changes gradients and activation scale.','Single seed, no paired user-cluster bootstrap interface in this proposal phase; external-work equivalence unverified.'], 'decision_if_supported':yes, 'decision_if_not_supported':no})\nnotes={\n 'mass_sum':'Primary candidate. Bounded sigmoid gates are summed without unit normalization; target-conditioned field mass is retained. Compare first with count_scaled, then mass_normalized. No new tensors; not an exact DIN reproduction.',\n 'mass_normalized':'Matched kernel control. Same sigmoid gates normalized by gate sum; unit total weight for nonempty retrieval. Isolates mass retention from switching softmax to sigmoid.',\n 'count_scaled':'Matched count control. Same normalized sigmoid weights multiplied by visible exposure count/2, matching sum weights at zero scores. Target-independent scale controls a count explanation; global-scale and optimization differences remain.',\n 'softmax_reference':'Faithful contemporaneous parent reference; exact original masked softmax path and initialization/tensors. Verify against g0-r0000-field_global. Same-seed rerun is reproducibility evidence, not an independent mechanism replicate.'}\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g0-r0000-field_global','variants':[{'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':dict(shared,pooling_mode=mode),'note':notes[name]} for name,file,role,mode in specs], 'knowledge_assessments':[\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-hiformer','decision':'used','rationale':'Read the pinned benchmark forward/tokenizer and the primary benchmark summary. History pooling followed by static/history/task token interaction is an inherited structural reference, not new local proof. The prior local model already has this broad pattern; original HiFormer text is unavailable.','transformed_mechanism':'Retain inherited post-pooling unified interaction, but change only field-wise retrieval normalization to test intensity-carrying summary units. No hierarchical HiFormer block is copied or newly introduced.','variant_names':[s[0] for s in specs],'nearest_work_difference':'Our inherited per-field target/context queries, five global summaries, shared small blocks and direct summary/static skip differ from the inspected event pooling and heterogeneous HiFormer blocks. The magnitude motivation is known from DIN; novelty unverified.','falsifier':'A mass_sum failure against matched normalization/count controls gives no support for the proposed intensity change; no claim about original HiFormer effectiveness follows.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-tokenmixer','decision':'considered','rationale':'Read pinned benchmark forward/tokenizer and mixing blocks plus benchmark section 2.3. Global/group tokenization and reversible mixing would change multiple mechanisms beyond the normalization limitation currently under test. Original method paper detail unavailable.','transformed_mechanism':'None; retain the existing interaction stack and token layout.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'No reversible token transport, global/chunk tokenizer or mean-token readout is added. This is not a TokenMixer reproduction or local comparison.','falsifier':'A later capacity/cost-matched tokenizer replacement could support revisiting this alternative; current pooling controls cannot establish its ineffectiveness.'}\n]}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Recorded prospective four-arm study in proposal.json before implementation.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\nRecorded prospective four-arm study in proposal.json before implementation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=json.loads(Path('proposal.json').read_text())\ns=Path('history_g0_r0000_field_global.py').read_text()\nend=s.index('\\\"\\\"\\\"',3)+3\ns='''\\\"\\\"\\\"Field-summary activation-mass study; performance not yet measured.\n\nInherited architecture: g0-r0000-field_global, source SHA256\n a3b2aa2e254ec5d995d9a4361592af40fb25a9c1c09023bc7d1223d2b5ccc125.\nOnly retrieval normalization changes; all parameter declarations and their order\nare inherited. Sigmoid sum retains activation mass, normalized sigmoid removes\nit, and count-scaled sigmoid substitutes visible count/2 for learned gate mass.\nThe unchanged softmax branch provides a contemporary reference.\n\nDIN primary text (arXiv:1706.06978v4, section 4.3) already motivates retaining\nactivation intensity. This is a bounded per-field adaptation within a small\nunified token model, not an originality claim or an exact DIN reproduction.\nPinned UniRank HiFormer and TokenMixer implementations were inspected as\narchitectural references; their original-paper equivalence is unverified.\nAll inputs, masks, loss and training/scoring belong to the frozen host contract.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"'''+s[end:]\nstart=s.index('CONFIG = ')\nend=s.index('\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass Interaction',start)\ns=s[:start]+'CONFIG = __CONFIG__'+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('field_retrieval=True, feedback_groups=False,\\\\n                 tower_hidden_units=',\\\"field_retrieval=True, feedback_groups=False,\\\\n                 pooling_mode=__DEFAULT_MODE__, tower_hidden_units=\\\")\ns=s.replace('        self.field_retrieval = field_retrieval', '''        if pooling_mode not in ('softmax', 'sigmoid_normalized',\n                                'sigmoid_count', 'sigmoid_sum'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown retrieval pooling mode')\n        if not field_retrieval or feedback_groups:\n            raise ValueError('This study fixes field retrieval and global pooling')\n        self.pooling_mode = pooling_mode\n        self.field_retrieval = field_retrieval''')\nstart=s.index('    @staticmethod\\\\n    def _masked_weights')\nend=s.index('\\\\n    def forward(self, inputs):',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''    def _masked_weights(self, scores, mask):\n        # scores: [B,F,L]; mask: [B,G,L]. Every arm uses exactly the\n        # same visible positions. Empty retrievals produce all-zero weights.\n        valid = mask[:, :, None, :].bool()\n        if self.pooling_mode == 'softmax':\n            # Exact arithmetic of the committed field_global parent.\n            weights = torch.softmax(scores[:, None].float().masked_fill(~valid, -1e9), dim=-1)\n            weights = weights * valid.to(weights.dtype)\n            return weights / weights.sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-9)\n        # Compute gates and reductions in FP32, before the inherited BF16\n        # value pooling. A fixed bound avoids unbounded exponential sums.\n        gates = torch.sigmoid(scores[:, None].float()) * valid.to(torch.float32)\n        if self.pooling_mode == 'sigmoid_sum':\n            return gates\n        mass = gates.sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        normalized = gates / mass.clamp_min(1e-9)\n        if self.pooling_mode == 'sigmoid_count':\n            # At zero score sigmoid(s)=1/2, so this equals sigmoid_sum.\n            # Unlike gate mass, visible count cannot depend on the target.\n            count = valid.to(torch.float32).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n            return normalized * (0.5 * count)\n        return normalized\n''' + s[end:]\nfor v in p['variants']:\n mode=v['config']['pooling_mode']\n out=s.replace('__CONFIG__',repr(v['config'])).replace('__DEFAULT_MODE__',repr(mode))\n assert '__CONFIG__' not in out and '__DEFAULT_MODE__' not in out\n Path(v['file']).write_text(out)\nprint('Wrote standalone modules:', ', '.join(v['file'] for v in p['variants']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
